config.js

{
  module: 'MMM-Images',
  position: 'fullscreen_above',   // fills the screen
  config: {
    imagePath: 'modules/MMM-Images/images',
    autoReturnHours: 0,           // 0 = disabled, or e.g. 2 for 2 hours
    gpioNext: 17,                 // Button A
    gpioMain: 27                  // Button B
  }
},





Also run:   Then run npm install inside the module folder.



Quick setup checklist

cd ~/MagicMirror/modules && git clone (or copy the folder)

npm install inside MMM-RecipePage

Wire your two buttons to GPIO17 and GPIO27 with internal pull-ups.

Add the module entry to config.js and restart MagicMirror.







Here’s a plan that integrates two physical GPIO buttons with a MagicMirror² module so you can flip between your regular MagicMirror dashboard and a “recipe slideshow” page. The idea is:

Button A = “Next recipe / enter recipe mode”

Button B = “Return to main screen”

Optional auto-return timer to go back after x hours.

Below is a full working outline you can copy into a module folder and adapt.

1. Hardware setup

Raspberry Pi running MagicMirror²

Two push-buttons wired between a GPIO pin and ground

e.g. GPIO17 for Button A

GPIO27 for Button B

Enable internal pull-ups so you don’t need extra resistors:

Connect the other side of each button to GND.
